<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  AnimaTree_NoRandomSpawn.xml            authored 2026-10-11
  Owner ruling 2026-10-11 (verbatim): "Anima tree is blocked on ALL biomes as a random occurrence.
  In Utinni, it should be a rare/unique entity that's placed quite intentionally (TBD)."
  Item: ANIMA_TREE_FIX_TAKES_THE_SIDE_DOOR.

  Plant_TreeAnima and the GenStepDef AnimaTrees are KEPT, so intentional placement later still works
  (the incident's treeGenStepDef points at AnimaTrees, so that def must stay). Only the three RANDOM
  routes are cut, each by a Conditional whose test is the Remove's own xpath (no match = silent no-op):
    1. Base_Player genSteps entry "AnimaTrees": every home map. Other generators (e.g. Caravan Adventures AncientMasterShrine, an authored site) are intentional placements and are left alone.
    2. StorytellerDef comps entry firing incident AnimaTreeSpawn (Core BaseStoryteller, OnOffCycle 15/15 days).
    3. BiomeDef preventGenSteps already lists AnimaTrees on Odyssey Glowforest: harmless once (1) is gone.
  Wild-plant spawning cannot place it: no BiomeDef wildPlants entry names Plant_TreeAnima (measured in
  Core/Royalty/Ideology/Odyssey Data, 2026-10-11).
-->
<Patch>
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/MapGeneratorDef[defName="Base_Player"]/genSteps/li[text()="AnimaTrees"]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationRemove">
      <xpath>/Defs/MapGeneratorDef[defName="Base_Player"]/genSteps/li[text()="AnimaTrees"]</xpath>
    </match>
  </Operation>
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/StorytellerDef/comps/li[incident="AnimaTreeSpawn"]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationRemove">
      <xpath>/Defs/StorytellerDef/comps/li[incident="AnimaTreeSpawn"]</xpath>
    </match>
  </Operation>
</Patch>
